WEBVTT

01:41.729 --> 01:48.870
[Genius Girlfriend]

01:49.430 --> 01:51.970
[Episode 14]

01:53.229 --> 01:54.479
Zhixia, let me tell you.

01:54.479 --> 01:56.400
You've come to the right person
for help picking out a new phone.

01:56.400 --> 01:57.350
I know all the phones and models

01:57.350 --> 01:58.680
like the back of my hand.

01:59.000 --> 01:59.789
This one.

01:59.840 --> 02:01.590
My idol is the spokesperson for it.

02:01.590 --> 02:02.560
It comes in 8 colors

02:02.560 --> 02:03.920
and has 105 breathing light effects.

02:03.920 --> 02:05.450
You can even customize
the light colors yourself.

02:05.450 --> 02:06.120
Isn't that cool?

02:05.540 --> 02:09.199
[AISUN; 1999 yuan]

02:09.470 --> 02:11.710
It's so pretty but a bit expensive.

02:11.960 --> 02:13.090
It's over my budget.

02:17.079 --> 02:18.210
What about this one?

02:18.630 --> 02:19.680
It's from a major brand

02:19.680 --> 02:21.240
with a piano-finish coating,

02:21.240 --> 02:23.040
and the price is reasonable too.

02:23.079 --> 02:24.340
This one is pretty too.

02:25.800 --> 02:26.860
How about this one?

02:27.190 --> 02:27.870
This one?

02:30.280 --> 02:32.280
I've never even heard of this brand.

02:32.370 --> 02:34.520
-Is this some knockoff...
-Sis.

02:36.840 --> 02:37.860
You have taste.

02:37.960 --> 02:39.560
You really have great taste.

02:39.800 --> 02:40.930
For all these years,

02:41.190 --> 02:42.520
I've been waiting for

02:43.000 --> 02:44.930
someone who truly understands it.

02:47.079 --> 02:48.140
Understands what?

02:51.750 --> 02:53.150
The Almighty King phone.

02:53.300 --> 02:54.190
It's about to become

02:54.190 --> 02:56.450
the future leader of the phone industry.

02:57.590 --> 02:59.470
Its performance is insane—blazing fast!

02:59.470 --> 03:01.240
And the battery life is unbelievable!

03:01.240 --> 03:03.430
Normally, you only need to
charge it for 2 hours,

03:03.430 --> 03:05.150
and you can use it nonstop
for a whole week.

03:05.150 --> 03:06.960
Plus, it's shockproof

03:07.630 --> 03:08.560
and waterproof.

03:12.150 --> 03:13.150
Don't believe me?

03:23.840 --> 03:25.280
See? Waterproof.

03:28.680 --> 03:30.190
And that's not even the best part.

03:30.190 --> 03:31.050
Watch closely!

03:34.840 --> 03:36.900
Have you ever seen a phone this tough?

03:37.680 --> 03:38.880
I just want to ask you—

03:39.360 --> 03:41.420
have you ever seen a phone this tough?

03:41.590 --> 03:44.079
All-in-one, all-powerful.

03:44.310 --> 03:46.910
The Almighty King phone is trustworthy.

03:47.360 --> 03:49.290
Choosing it is the right decision!

03:53.360 --> 03:55.870
Sir, I don't need to
crack walnuts with it or anything.

03:55.870 --> 03:58.200
I just need it to
make calls and send texts.

03:58.240 --> 04:00.360
The main thing is,
the price fits my budget.

04:00.360 --> 04:02.290
I want to buy one for my brother too.

04:02.960 --> 04:04.360
Sis, if you buy two today,

04:04.800 --> 04:06.200
I'll give you a discount.

04:07.840 --> 04:09.640
Are you sure? The Almighty King?

04:14.120 --> 04:16.360
[Emile]

04:19.480 --> 04:20.339
What are these?

04:21.560 --> 04:24.220
We can afford 2 of these phones
within my budget.

04:24.240 --> 04:25.680
Don't wait until after New Year's.

04:25.680 --> 04:27.280
Let's share the good things.

04:30.270 --> 04:32.630
These aren't...

04:33.159 --> 04:34.870
These aren't some knockoffs, are they?

04:34.870 --> 04:36.800
They're the Almighty King phones.

04:37.330 --> 04:40.300
Bet you didn't know that.
Not only do they have great performance,

04:40.300 --> 04:42.030
but they're also built to last.

04:42.750 --> 04:45.310
What you're really paying for
in an expensive phone is the brand value.

04:45.310 --> 04:47.110
I don't think that's necessary.

04:48.220 --> 04:50.420
You really don't...

04:57.159 --> 04:57.950
Can they be returned?

04:57.950 --> 04:58.880
Why return them?

05:00.720 --> 05:03.560
If you return them...
you can buy a more expensive one.

05:03.560 --> 05:04.510
One you like more.

05:04.510 --> 05:06.310
Plus, I might get a new phone
for the New Year.

05:06.310 --> 05:08.970
I don't really need a phone
that badly right now.

05:20.000 --> 05:22.750
But I picked these colors carefully.

05:23.000 --> 05:24.240
Gold represents autumn,

05:24.240 --> 05:25.840
and blue represents summer.

05:27.680 --> 05:29.720
Since you don't like it, Brother,

05:29.720 --> 05:31.300
I'll just return it.

05:31.600 --> 05:33.800
Okay, okay, okay. I like it. I like it.

05:34.120 --> 05:36.450
T-This is the Almighty King phone, right?

05:39.360 --> 05:40.870
I've heard of this phone.

05:44.950 --> 05:46.550
It can really smash walnuts?

05:49.600 --> 05:51.260
I'll smash it with yours then.

05:57.560 --> 05:58.920
I-It's so sturdy.

06:15.800 --> 06:16.830
Hello, Jiang.

06:16.950 --> 06:18.060
Guess who this is.

06:27.920 --> 06:28.510
Hello?

06:29.160 --> 06:30.090
Is it Lin Zhixia?

06:31.310 --> 06:32.870
How did you know it was me?

06:34.600 --> 06:36.060
Didn't you ask me to guess?

06:36.800 --> 06:37.659
I just guessed.

06:38.920 --> 06:40.630
This is my number. Save it.

06:40.920 --> 06:42.190
You're my best friend.

06:42.480 --> 06:44.409
You're the first person I've told.

06:46.680 --> 06:48.610
Let me tell you something amazing.

06:48.680 --> 06:50.070
When I was choosing my phone number today,

06:50.070 --> 06:51.360
I saw one

06:51.560 --> 06:52.950
where the last digits happened to

06:52.950 --> 06:54.630
match your birthday.

06:55.040 --> 06:56.170
Isn't that amazing?

06:57.270 --> 07:00.350
[Answer]

06:59.070 --> 07:01.800
Too bad there wasn't one
ending with my birthday.

07:04.870 --> 07:06.680
That's a bit of a pity.

07:07.360 --> 07:09.800
But it's already lucky enough, isn't it?

07:09.870 --> 07:12.130
And this number is very easy to remember.

07:13.190 --> 07:14.000
It's alright.

07:14.360 --> 07:16.560
I remember other people's numbers too.

07:17.070 --> 07:19.000
So the contacts feature on your phone

07:19.000 --> 07:20.530
is basically useless, huh?

07:23.190 --> 07:24.000
Lin Zhixia,

07:25.000 --> 07:27.750
what name did you save me as?

07:29.160 --> 07:30.070
Jiang Yubai.

07:32.720 --> 07:34.750
Well, good friends

07:34.920 --> 07:36.920
usually give each other nicknames—

07:36.950 --> 07:39.040
a name that only the two of them

07:39.040 --> 07:40.000
would know.

07:45.310 --> 07:47.040
I'll have to think of a good one.

07:49.360 --> 07:50.480
I gotta go.

07:50.630 --> 07:52.360
I need to call my other friends.

07:54.920 --> 07:56.560
Alright then, bye-bye.

07:57.190 --> 07:57.920
Bye-bye.

08:03.610 --> 08:06.370
[Hang up]

08:15.410 --> 08:29.590
[Contacts: J-J-J-Jiang]

08:16.070 --> 08:16.870
Jiang...

08:29.310 --> 08:30.000
Son.

08:30.630 --> 08:31.600
Look at the time.

08:31.600 --> 08:33.059
Why aren't you asleep yet?

08:33.549 --> 08:34.549
Mom, you're back.

08:34.720 --> 08:36.120
Why are you home so late today?

08:36.120 --> 08:37.549
Well, business has been busy lately,

08:37.549 --> 08:39.350
so I've had more client dinners.

08:39.360 --> 08:40.320
But you.

08:40.360 --> 08:41.600
Look at you.

08:42.720 --> 08:44.380
Studying this late every day.

08:44.910 --> 08:47.640
You're not getting enough sleep.
That's no good.

08:47.720 --> 08:49.320
Finals are coming up.

08:49.440 --> 08:50.910
I need to prepare well.

08:52.550 --> 08:54.480
Your grades are already very good.

08:54.480 --> 08:56.320
Don't push yourself so hard.

08:57.030 --> 08:57.870
That won't do.

08:58.120 --> 08:59.080
Everyone else is working hard.

08:59.080 --> 09:00.360
I can't afford to slack off.

09:00.360 --> 09:02.560
I'm hoping to beat my previous ranking.

09:05.120 --> 09:06.630
Look at you. You're already so tall,

09:06.630 --> 09:09.080
yet you still talk like a kid.

09:10.720 --> 09:11.790
Other kids

09:11.790 --> 09:14.080
need to be pushed and pushed to study.

09:14.390 --> 09:15.390
But you?

09:15.630 --> 09:16.550
You're the opposite.

09:16.550 --> 09:18.200
I have to push you to rest.

09:20.550 --> 09:21.610
Alright, alright.

09:22.000 --> 09:22.910
I won't nag you anymore.

09:22.910 --> 09:23.910
Go to sleep early.

09:27.630 --> 09:28.840
Keep track of the time yourself, alright?

09:28.840 --> 09:29.840
I know, Mom.

09:43.250 --> 09:44.200
Jiang...

09:54.000 --> 09:55.120
You want to study me

09:55.530 --> 09:55.970
[The Human Observation Diary
is a preliminary research review]

09:55.600 --> 09:58.080
because I am an ordinary human?

09:56.000 --> 09:56.820
[on ordinary humans' thinking modes.]

09:58.120 --> 09:58.920
That's right.

09:59.320 --> 10:00.790
I feel like half of

10:01.360 --> 10:03.620
my competitive streak was shaped by you.

10:06.750 --> 10:08.150
I will admit my mistakes and correct them.

10:08.150 --> 10:09.750
I'm apologizing to you right now.

10:09.750 --> 10:11.410
Jiang Yubai is not an ordinary human—

10:11.410 --> 10:13.840
he's a great genius.

10:17.150 --> 10:19.260
[Contacts; Name: No Ordinary Human]

10:36.280 --> 10:41.080
[Contacts; Name: No Ordinary Human]

10:49.390 --> 10:52.190
[Astronomy Club]

11:08.080 --> 11:08.870
Jin Baihui?

11:09.440 --> 11:10.080
Hi.

11:10.080 --> 11:11.010
You really came.

11:11.910 --> 11:13.120
Welcome to the astronomy club.

11:13.120 --> 11:14.520
Feel free to look around.

11:36.840 --> 11:38.170
What are you working on?

11:38.870 --> 11:40.390
I'm calibrating this dome.

11:40.390 --> 11:41.240
I want to watch

11:41.240 --> 11:43.390
the meteor shower footage
we recorded earlier.

11:43.390 --> 11:44.150
A meteor shower?

11:44.150 --> 11:44.750
Yeah.

11:45.270 --> 11:46.730
Want to watch it together?

11:47.200 --> 11:47.910
Sure.

11:49.440 --> 11:51.040
This meteor shower happened

11:51.120 --> 11:53.250
around 10:30 PM the night before last.

11:54.630 --> 11:57.080
First, there was a partial lunar eclipse,

11:58.240 --> 12:00.000
then the meteor shower reached its peak.

12:00.000 --> 12:00.750
Have a seat.

12:02.150 --> 12:04.910
In the end, they formed a rare phenomenon:

12:05.480 --> 12:08.480
an eclipsed moonrise
accompanied by a meteor shower.

12:09.650 --> 12:11.440
Since this dome is a simulator,

12:11.970 --> 12:14.970
seeing it in person
would've been even more stunning.

12:22.270 --> 12:23.800
Where is the meteor shower?

12:24.070 --> 12:25.000
Wait a moment.

12:33.630 --> 12:34.360
I see it.

12:49.790 --> 12:50.990
Are you making a wish?

13:11.670 --> 13:13.470
Why did the meteors stop moving?

13:13.720 --> 13:15.180
Weren't you making a wish?

13:15.320 --> 13:16.380
I paused it for you.

13:50.870 --> 13:52.120
If there's nothing else,

13:51.850 --> 13:54.340
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

13:52.790 --> 13:53.990
that's all for today.

13:59.600 --> 14:01.000
Let me say a few more things.

14:01.000 --> 14:02.400
Put down your pens first.

14:04.150 --> 14:05.150
Our experimental class

14:05.150 --> 14:07.120
is the best group of students
in the entire grade.

14:07.120 --> 14:08.580
There is no doubt about it.

14:08.910 --> 14:10.630
So you've already gotten used to

14:10.630 --> 14:11.890
being praised as smart

14:11.960 --> 14:13.480
and getting better grades
on your report cards

14:13.480 --> 14:14.440
than everyone else.

14:14.440 --> 14:15.150
But...

14:16.120 --> 14:19.030
the final exams can't be handled
on autopilot.

14:20.000 --> 14:22.150
The subjects you feel most confident in

14:22.150 --> 14:24.150
might be where others overtake you.

14:25.360 --> 14:27.420
The questions you think you got right

14:27.510 --> 14:29.200
may be the very ones that drag down

14:29.200 --> 14:30.200
your ranking.

14:30.910 --> 14:34.480
So being in the experimental class
is not a free pass.

14:34.840 --> 14:37.200
You have to be more careful than ever.

14:38.670 --> 14:41.510
Also, our class has
the rank-based elimination system.

14:41.510 --> 14:43.030
If the sum of your two exam scores

14:43.030 --> 14:46.120
falls out of the top 50 in the grade,
you'll automatically be transferred out.

14:46.120 --> 14:47.120
You all know this.

14:47.120 --> 14:49.250
When that happens, no one can help you.

14:49.390 --> 14:51.200
So, with the holiday coming up soon,

14:51.200 --> 14:52.910
I don't want the exam results

14:53.120 --> 14:54.320
to ruin your New Year.

14:56.080 --> 14:58.750
So do your best
and take the exams seriously, okay?

14:58.750 --> 14:59.390
Okay.

14:59.600 --> 15:00.320
Okay.

15:00.340 --> 15:00.950
Okay.

15:00.980 --> 15:01.410
Okay.

15:01.510 --> 15:02.840
Louder. Okay?

15:02.870 --> 15:04.200
Okay!

15:02.920 --> 15:05.950
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

15:04.200 --> 15:05.080
Do your best.

15:05.080 --> 15:06.680
Good luck. Don't be nervous.

15:12.600 --> 15:14.530
Brother, what's for dinner today?

15:17.960 --> 15:18.750
Not at home?

15:47.120 --> 15:48.920
How did this book end up with you?

15:51.270 --> 15:54.840
Jin Baihui came over
and returned this book a few days ago.

15:56.670 --> 15:58.120
Her dad tore it up.

15:58.720 --> 15:59.510
Why?

16:04.750 --> 16:06.670
She didn't do well
on her last monthly exam.

16:06.670 --> 16:09.480
Her dad thought
she wasn't focusing on her studies.

16:09.480 --> 16:11.150
So giving her this book was your way of

16:11.150 --> 16:13.010
intentionally distracting her.

16:13.150 --> 16:14.440
What do you mean she didn't do well?

16:14.440 --> 16:16.150
She's still in the top few in the grade

16:16.150 --> 16:18.240
and has always studied hard.

16:19.120 --> 16:20.630
In her parents' eyes—

16:21.320 --> 16:23.180
actually, in many people's eyes—

16:23.790 --> 16:25.250
if you don't come in first,

16:25.910 --> 16:27.310
that's a failure in life.

16:28.610 --> 16:29.670
Tearing up the book

16:30.080 --> 16:32.280
is just an extreme way of expressing it.

16:34.080 --> 16:36.210
Is being first really that important?

16:36.840 --> 16:38.550
Jiang Yubai had always wanted to beat me

16:38.550 --> 16:39.750
and come in first too.

16:40.000 --> 16:41.730
But grades aren't everything.

16:44.200 --> 16:46.000
Only people...

16:48.670 --> 16:52.130
who've actually gotten first place
have the right to say that.

16:57.000 --> 16:58.660
Anyway, don't worry about it.

16:59.790 --> 17:01.630
And don't tell Jin Baihui either.

17:01.630 --> 17:03.360
She already feels bad about it.

17:08.480 --> 17:11.280
Ten minutes left until the exam ends.

17:11.920 --> 17:13.319
Please manage your time.

17:54.790 --> 17:55.720
I did pretty well.

17:55.720 --> 17:56.440
Yeah.

17:56.440 --> 17:57.030
Let's go.

17:57.030 --> 17:57.680
Let's go.

18:13.590 --> 18:15.190
I was careless. So careless.

18:15.550 --> 18:17.000
I should've gotten full marks
on my combined science.

18:17.000 --> 18:19.480
God knows what obscure detail
cost me 2 points.

18:19.480 --> 18:20.310
Shen,

18:21.030 --> 18:22.550
if I hadn't made a careless mistake,

18:22.550 --> 18:24.350
you wouldn't have caught up with me.

18:24.350 --> 18:26.400
Then you'd better be careful next time.

18:26.400 --> 18:27.860
After all, the same excuse

18:28.240 --> 18:29.310
won't work twice.

18:32.150 --> 18:32.750
By the way,

18:32.750 --> 18:33.550
I heard

18:34.440 --> 18:37.240
those starch sausages
aren't good for your brain.

18:37.640 --> 18:38.830
Give me a break.

18:41.310 --> 18:43.200
Lin Zhixia actually
didn't get first place?

18:43.200 --> 18:44.600
That doesn't seem right.

18:45.590 --> 18:48.120
Could it be
that everything happening lately

18:48.350 --> 18:49.350
distracted her?

18:51.110 --> 18:53.110
But she shouldn't have dropped to fifth.

18:53.110 --> 18:55.310
I'm only 4 places behind Lin Zhixia?

18:55.920 --> 18:57.440
This is so encouraging!

18:58.580 --> 18:59.510
What about Tang?

19:04.440 --> 19:05.680
Our dead last, Tang Tingting.

19:05.680 --> 19:06.830
She's always been consistent.

19:06.830 --> 19:08.560
She dropped a few places again.

19:11.750 --> 19:12.400
Let's go.

19:12.830 --> 19:13.400
Go.

19:27.750 --> 19:28.810
Congratulations.

19:29.110 --> 19:29.920
You did great.

19:31.930 --> 19:32.980
[Grade 10 Final Exam Rankings]

19:33.000 --> 19:33.740
[1; Jin Baihui] [2; Jiang Yubai]

19:33.770 --> 19:34.670
[3; Zhao Li] [4; Li Yuanyuan]

19:34.700 --> 19:35.990
[5; Lin Zhixia] [6; Wang Xinrui]

19:43.960 --> 19:46.690
The formula
must have been written incorrectly.

19:49.290 --> 19:50.880
Why were 2 points deducted?

20:05.640 --> 20:07.400
Tang, you're really bad at
science subjects.

20:07.400 --> 20:08.510
Especially math.

20:09.000 --> 20:11.570
I could score higher than you
with my eyes closed.

20:11.570 --> 20:12.270
Get lost.

20:13.000 --> 20:14.800
I'm not in the mood to talk to you.

20:21.920 --> 20:22.720
Lin Zhixia,

20:22.830 --> 20:24.270
can I borrow your math paper

20:24.270 --> 20:25.400
to check my answers?

20:28.270 --> 20:28.960
Thanks.

20:36.830 --> 20:39.030
So that's what the last question meant.

20:39.480 --> 20:41.480
I didn't even understand it before.

20:43.830 --> 20:44.720
Wait a minute.

20:45.590 --> 20:47.310
You got
all the long-answer questions right.

20:47.310 --> 20:49.040
Then where did you lose points?

20:56.440 --> 20:57.830
How did you get this question wrong?

20:57.830 --> 20:58.890
Even I got it right.

20:59.350 --> 21:00.160
And this one.

21:03.940 --> 21:05.270
I... I... well...

21:07.310 --> 21:09.400
I-I lost focus during the exam.

21:13.160 --> 21:13.960
Thanks.

21:51.000 --> 21:51.920
Lin Zhixia.

21:53.790 --> 21:54.850
Why did you do this?

21:57.040 --> 21:57.880
What's wrong?

21:59.920 --> 22:01.720
Math is your strongest subject.

22:02.510 --> 22:06.440
There's no way you'd get the first 2
multiple-choice questions wrong.

22:07.920 --> 22:09.780
You did it on purpose, didn't you?

22:10.160 --> 22:11.030
I didn't.

22:20.060 --> 22:21.350
Do you think you have to hold back

22:21.350 --> 22:22.310
for me to win?

22:24.000 --> 22:25.480
Are you taking pity on me?

22:25.830 --> 22:27.160
Do you think I'm stupid?

22:29.510 --> 22:30.640
During this whole final exam period,

22:30.640 --> 22:32.970
I studied until after midnight every day.

22:33.750 --> 22:36.080
And yet, what I won
was a fake competition.

22:37.920 --> 22:40.030
I don't study for exam rankings...

22:40.030 --> 22:40.830
I do!

22:45.110 --> 22:45.880
Okay?

22:47.010 --> 22:52.930
[Toward a Sea of Stars,
Chasing Our Dreams]

22:56.840 --> 23:01.810
[Toward a Sea of Stars,
Chasing Our Dreams]

23:28.110 --> 23:30.400
Come on. Open your books to page 67.

23:35.420 --> 23:37.060
[A hundred-year undertaking
begins with education]

24:08.000 --> 24:09.060
What are you doing?

24:10.510 --> 24:11.680
I'm observing you.

24:12.240 --> 24:13.750
I'm planning to write

24:13.920 --> 24:16.180
a Human Observation Diary about you too.

24:17.070 --> 24:18.600
And what have you observed?

24:19.830 --> 24:20.720
I've observed

24:21.160 --> 24:22.310
that Lin Zhixia has

24:22.590 --> 24:24.790
taken a little detour on her way

24:24.880 --> 24:27.340
to becoming more emotionally intelligent.

24:28.510 --> 24:30.770
To help her friend improve her rankings,

24:31.000 --> 24:33.750
she deliberately held back on the exams.

24:34.480 --> 24:36.240
But because of her clumsy tricks,

24:36.240 --> 24:37.500
she gave herself away.

24:41.480 --> 24:43.440
I thought I was helping Jin Baihui.

24:44.310 --> 24:47.000
But I can't understand why she got angry.

24:50.530 --> 24:51.990
You know what, Lin Zhixia?

24:52.790 --> 24:53.850
Although this time

24:53.880 --> 24:56.590
you deliberately held back
so I could outrank you,

24:56.590 --> 24:57.350
to me,

24:57.350 --> 24:59.550
this isn't something to be happy about.

25:02.310 --> 25:04.370
I think Jin Baihui feels the same way.

25:07.030 --> 25:09.430
She didn't do well
on the last monthly exam.

25:10.110 --> 25:13.350
Maybe she spent this entire month
studying harder than ever.

25:13.350 --> 25:15.200
Every time she felt like
she couldn't keep going,

25:15.200 --> 25:16.440
she probably thought,

25:16.440 --> 25:17.400
"Maybe if I try a little harder,

25:17.400 --> 25:18.860
I can surpass Lin Zhixia."

25:19.110 --> 25:20.720
And she'd be motivated again.

25:20.720 --> 25:22.520
But she never saw you as an enemy,

25:23.160 --> 25:24.480
only as an opponent.

25:29.590 --> 25:33.070
That's a form of admiration,
recognition, and respect.

25:37.590 --> 25:39.320
Just like in a basketball game.

25:39.350 --> 25:42.150
Whenever the ace players
from both sides face off,

25:42.160 --> 25:43.890
the audience stands and cheers

25:44.270 --> 25:46.000
because everyone expects

25:46.000 --> 25:47.460
a true, all-out showdown.

25:48.510 --> 25:49.680
No matter who wins or loses,

25:49.680 --> 25:52.010
the players exchange jerseys afterward.

25:52.480 --> 25:54.350
It's a truly wonderful moment.

26:00.640 --> 26:01.480
It's like...

26:02.750 --> 26:04.200
you've prepared yourself

26:04.200 --> 26:06.200
extremely thoroughly for a match,

26:06.550 --> 26:08.680
but your opponent suddenly forfeits.

26:08.830 --> 26:10.360
Would you still feel happy?

26:44.960 --> 26:46.920
This is the latest math practice test

26:46.920 --> 26:48.480
based on the Grade 10 curriculum,

26:48.480 --> 26:50.030
available in bookstores.

26:52.440 --> 26:53.240
Jin Baihui,

26:53.830 --> 26:54.830
I'd like to invite you

26:54.830 --> 26:57.490
to compete with me again
during the lunch break.

26:58.440 --> 26:59.200
I promise

26:59.640 --> 27:01.240
I'll give it my all this time.

27:19.440 --> 27:20.750
Then eat faster,

27:20.920 --> 27:23.180
or we won't have enough time for the test.

27:28.280 --> 27:32.100
[Pursue Knowledge, Seek Truth;
Practice Diligently, Foster Innovation]

27:29.000 --> 27:29.830
Lin Zhixia,

27:30.750 --> 27:32.010
do your best this time.

27:32.680 --> 27:34.510
Don't worry. I won't hold back.

27:42.530 --> 27:46.920
[VS]

27:46.780 --> 27:49.940
♪ The world is limitless colour puzzle ♪

27:50.210 --> 27:53.340
♪ I have the wildest dreams;
never fitting in ♪

27:53.790 --> 27:56.680
♪ The formula in my mind
is messed up and reorganized ♪

27:57.270 --> 28:00.270
♪ Is loneliness my only talent? ♪

28:00.940 --> 28:04.610
♪ Hide in the midsummer tree shade;
what's waiting for my answer? ♪

28:04.970 --> 28:07.040
♪ The breeze blows past my cheeks ♪

28:07.860 --> 28:10.660
♪ How do I solve for
the unexpected variables? ♪

28:11.100 --> 28:13.880
♪ At the most splendid moment ♪

28:14.610 --> 28:17.730
♪ Running and waiting for my exploration ♪

28:17.960 --> 28:20.920
♪ The unknown is so fascinating ♪

28:21.430 --> 28:23.600
♪ Young me stood on tiptoes ♪

28:24.070 --> 28:28.050
♪ Everything is transparent;
time is too light ♪

28:28.790 --> 28:29.270
♪ Natural deduction ♪

28:28.920 --> 28:31.520
I think I did even better
than on the final exam.

28:31.550 --> 28:32.350
Me too.

29:13.070 --> 29:18.280
[Pursue Knowledge, Seek Truth;
Practice Diligently, Foster Innovation]

29:32.680 --> 29:34.140
Jin Baihui's score is out.

29:35.140 --> 29:37.000
-How many points did she get?
-What's her score?

29:37.000 --> 29:37.770
No way.

29:38.110 --> 29:39.310
148?

29:39.400 --> 29:40.590
148.

29:40.750 --> 29:42.640
That's 2 points higher
than her final exam score.

29:42.640 --> 29:43.400
Yeah.

29:43.640 --> 29:44.590
So impressive.

29:44.830 --> 29:46.000
-She only missed one fill-in-the-blank.
-So impressive.

29:46.000 --> 29:47.310
That's incredible.

29:47.960 --> 29:49.220
What about Lin Zhixia?

29:50.000 --> 29:51.660
Lin Zhixia's score is out too.

30:11.680 --> 30:12.590
First place.

30:13.270 --> 30:15.350
Baihui, you did really well this time.

30:15.350 --> 30:17.070
Your hard work paid off.

30:17.310 --> 30:19.310
Hard work always pays off, you know?

30:19.880 --> 30:20.550
See?

30:20.550 --> 30:22.240
Mom and Dad were right to stop you from

30:22.240 --> 30:23.350
wasting time on those useless

30:23.350 --> 30:24.160
extracurricular activities.

30:24.160 --> 30:26.310
Otherwise, how could you have achieved
such a great ranking?

30:26.310 --> 30:27.550
I think she lost 5 points in Chinese

30:27.550 --> 30:29.480
because of her essay.

30:29.480 --> 30:30.980
These 4 points off in math...

30:30.980 --> 30:33.510
Actually, I didn't get
first place this time.

30:35.790 --> 30:36.720
What do you mean?

30:36.960 --> 30:37.830
What happened?

30:40.310 --> 30:41.310
Lin Zhixia let me

30:41.740 --> 30:43.270
take first place this time.

30:44.590 --> 30:45.450
Let you take it?

30:49.830 --> 30:52.200
Are you still happy now?

30:58.750 --> 31:00.950
What's the point of being first anyway?

31:00.960 --> 31:01.960
What's the point?

31:03.270 --> 31:05.400
In this society, except for first place,

31:05.400 --> 31:07.510
second place is
no different from last place.

31:07.510 --> 31:09.400
In a competition,
the runner-up is just a loser.

31:09.400 --> 31:10.640
Don't you understand that?

31:10.640 --> 31:12.000
But does that mean
all the effort a runner-up puts in

31:12.000 --> 31:12.880
is just a waste?

31:12.880 --> 31:15.030
The college entrance exam
only cares about the result.

31:15.030 --> 31:16.160
For that result,

31:16.160 --> 31:18.350
your dad and I
have kept making sacrifices.

31:18.350 --> 31:19.310
Back then, for you...

31:19.310 --> 31:19.960
Yes!

31:21.000 --> 31:22.790
Back then, you gave up your jobs

31:22.790 --> 31:24.310
to accompany me to Beijing.

31:24.310 --> 31:25.350
When I couldn't keep up
in the gifted class,

31:25.350 --> 31:26.350
you came back with me.

31:26.350 --> 31:27.640
I know that.

31:28.350 --> 31:29.680
I'm very grateful.

31:31.030 --> 31:33.350
But I gave it my absolute all back then.

31:35.270 --> 31:36.920
I slept less than 5 hours a day

31:36.920 --> 31:39.520
and spent the rest of my time
doing test papers.

31:40.110 --> 31:41.440
I felt like I was close to

31:41.640 --> 31:43.570
breaking down mentally back then.

31:44.160 --> 31:46.000
But why did you still keep pushing me?

31:46.000 --> 31:47.790
You two are ordinary people too!

31:47.790 --> 31:49.640
Baihui, who was pushing you?

31:49.830 --> 31:53.030
I try my hardest every single day,
every single moment.

31:53.440 --> 31:55.550
But everyone's limit is different.

31:57.200 --> 31:59.330
After I found out Lin Zhixia let me win,

32:00.030 --> 32:01.760
I even competed with her again.

32:01.920 --> 32:02.830
And the result?

32:05.440 --> 32:06.440
I just lost.

32:07.350 --> 32:08.680
She got a perfect score.

32:10.110 --> 32:11.640
But so what?

32:13.270 --> 32:15.030
At No. 1 High School, there's Lin Zhixia—

32:15.030 --> 32:16.550
and in this world, there are

32:16.550 --> 32:18.440
countless more people
who are even better than Lin Zhixia.

32:18.440 --> 32:20.370
When does the comparing ever stop?

32:29.180 --> 32:29.830
Dad.

32:31.510 --> 32:32.200
Mom.

32:34.350 --> 32:36.210
You probably didn't even notice—

32:37.440 --> 32:38.440
this time I scored

32:39.480 --> 32:41.610
a full 20 points higher than last time.

32:44.000 --> 32:45.060
Every single point

32:46.250 --> 32:48.720
was earned with all my effort.

32:56.960 --> 32:58.070
So from now on...

33:00.290 --> 33:02.020
I'll only compete with myself.

33:24.250 --> 33:26.380
[Grade 10 Math
Semester 1 Required Module 1]

33:26.400 --> 33:28.640
[Comprehensive Test; Total Mock Test; 3]

33:30.320 --> 33:32.220
Now, I can't even remember

33:33.290 --> 33:36.080
[Grade 10 Math
Semester 1 Required Module 1]

33:33.460 --> 33:35.900
what mindset I had back then

33:36.100 --> 33:38.160
[Comprehensive Test; Total Mock Test; 3]

33:36.310 --> 33:39.710
when I deliberately got
2 multiple-choice questions wrong.

33:39.790 --> 33:41.510
I think I simply felt

33:42.180 --> 33:44.640
that Jin Baihui was
under too much pressure.

33:46.090 --> 33:47.090
In the rematch,

33:47.880 --> 33:48.790
she lost to me—

33:49.940 --> 33:51.870
but that gave her more peace of mind

33:52.220 --> 33:54.280
than winning first place would have.

33:54.880 --> 33:56.340
It also made me understand

33:57.550 --> 33:58.610
that true respect

33:59.030 --> 34:03.970
[Jin Baihui] [Lin Zhixia]

33:59.250 --> 34:00.450
is not about yielding

34:01.310 --> 34:03.570
but going all out when facing each other.

34:05.530 --> 34:06.610
Fortunately,

34:07.610 --> 34:10.210
my little scheme—smart or not—
finally helped

34:10.460 --> 34:13.190
Jin Baihui let go of
what had been weighing on her.

34:14.770 --> 34:15.820
From then on,

34:16.500 --> 34:17.690
her biggest rival

34:17.820 --> 34:18.760
was no longer me,

34:20.000 --> 34:21.360
but her past self.

34:21.179 --> 34:27.840
[Contacts: L-L-L-L-Lin Zhixia]

34:27.870 --> 34:33.600
[Contacts: High-EQ Human]

34:49.949 --> 34:53.199
[Go All Out, Friendship Forever]
